        "original_id": "c62b1267-1ef6-57cc-bffc-527eea17e25e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Steven Wilson, Lunch, Martin Bisi\n- Bands and Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth, Death Valley '69'\n- Publications and Rankings: Rolling Stone, Spin\n\nFacts:\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956, and he is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974, and he is a Swedish musician.\n- In 1984, Martin Bisi recorded the song \"Death Valley '69.\"\n- The song \"Death Valley '69\" was written and sung by Thurston Moore and the New York musician Lunch.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of the collaboration Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo at number 33 on its \"Greatest Guitarists of All Time\" list.\n- In May 2012, Spin ranked Thurston Moore and his Sonic Youth bandmate Lee Ranaldo together at number 1 in a staff-selected top 100 ranking.",
